finding: 0cf5ee79's allocation evidence is false: its claim that every window, including the refused one, reads 0 bytes comes from discarded samples. diagnostics/first-person-allocation/allocation.ts clears window.sites on a tier-up unless retainOptimizedSites:true. Independently running sampleAllocation(query-allocation.entry.ts,{warm:1800,retainOptimizedSites:true}) twice on HEAD produced 9712 B / 15 samples at step2 (solver/step.ts:8:21), with readJointEventUserData optimizing in the first window; the other windows were 0. The same diagnostic on the before tree s8A at warm 1800 had no optimizations and all windows 0; HEAD at warm 2400 had no optimizations and all windows 0, with the allocating control observed. Increasing warm-up is permitted by CONTRIBUTING, and these results do not establish steady allocation, but they contradict the stated evidence used to justify that change. Smallest correction: retain refused-window sites when diagnosing, correct the zero-byte claim, and explicitly distinguish the observed transient allocation/tier-up from the qualified zero-byte steady windows; do not represent the sampler's cleared sites as a measurement. No kernel equivalence defect found in the independently inspected paths and targeted tests.
